  "notes": "Cream mid-rise apartment block (spec says 3 floors and is trusted here, but the iso clearly reads as FOUR storeys of balcony bays - flag for the critic loop). Left edge is a stairwell column with one window per floor; the centre facade has two bays per floor of tall windows fronted by shallow Juliet balconies with curved black bombe wrought-iron rails (terraces entry uses non-schema floors/at/depth fields - schema gap: terraces have no position/repeat control, and the curved rail profile is not expressible). The right corner section alternates beige stone-block cladding bands with cream stucco per floor and wraps onto the right facade. Recessed near-black entrance door with house number 2225, a copper mailbox and a round white globe sconce high on the wall (number plaque + mailbox are schema gaps). Roof: flat with deep cream cornice/fascia, small stair-bulkhead box and an AC unit on top (schema ac prop is facade-mounted only - roof AC noted here). Frontage: beige stone-block garden wall with light joints and an OPEN entry walkway (no gate leaf), big cream slab path, and instead of a grass verge a dark-brown mulch garden bed (#5c3b32) edged with white rocks (#dbd0b5), terracotta pots with succulents and small planters; palm trees overhang and cast large frond shadows on the facade (prop factory pending). Beyond the wall the ground is plain warm-grey concrete (#968f7f). Sampled colours from 12x9 grids 2026-07-03."
